WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:00.880
INTRO:
Can you guess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.120
what the third largest automaker in the world is?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:10.800
Volkswagen? GM? Daimler? While those are all&nbsp;
great guesses and would usually be correct, we’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.920
not living in normal times. Last week, the third&nbsp;
most valued automaker in the world was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:37.760
Rivian. Rivian peaked at a valuation of $150&nbsp;
billion which is more than Volkswagen. Volkswagen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.640
generally delivers a cool 10 million cars per&nbsp;
year. Considering this, how many cars do you think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:50.160
Rivian delivers? 8 million? 5 million? Well, the&nbsp;
answer is actually a whopping 156 pickup trucks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.680
Now, I don’t wanna bag on Rivian because they’ve&nbsp;
worked super hard on their pickup truck over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.120
the past decade and they’ve had to cross so many&nbsp;
hurdles to get to market. Moreover, they actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.760
have a great working product unlike some other&nbsp;
notable competitors. So, there’s nothing wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.080
with the company Rivian, but there’s no doubt&nbsp;
that there’s something seriously screwed up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.440
the stock Rivian. So, here’s the story of Rivian&nbsp;
and how they became the epitome of the EV bubble.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.720
QUIET BEGINNINGS:&nbsp;

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.840
Taking a look back, when Rivian was founded in&nbsp;
2009, most people didn’t really care about EVs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.840
EVs were completely impractical due to their low&nbsp;
range and high cost. Hybrids were starting to pick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.960
up steam but this was only in what most would&nbsp;
consider the nerd community. So, Rivian didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.760
particularly have a bright outlook out the gate,&nbsp;
but that didn’t stop a man named Robert Scaringe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:47.840
or RJ from taking the risk anyway. At the time, RJ&nbsp;
was only 26 years old and he had spent his whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.720
adult life in academia. RJ had a bachelors in&nbsp;
mechanical engineering from Rensselaer Polytechnic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.000
Institute and a PHD in mechanical engineering from&nbsp;
MIT. But instead of continuing on in the regular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.640
path and getting a job, after graduation, RJ&nbsp;
returned to his home state of Florida and founded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.680
Mainstream Motors. Some sources say that RJ came&nbsp;
up with the capital himself, but at 26 with most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.451
of his life spent in academia, it’s not likely&nbsp;
that he would’ve been able to come up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.451 --> 00:02:16.240
car company levels of startup capital.&nbsp;
I’m sure RJ put in every penny he had,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.760
but most of the money for initial development came&nbsp;
from the Florida government. You see, RJ’s father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.640
Robert Scaringe Sr. was a business owner himself&nbsp;
who ran a company called Mainstream Engineering.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.440
I think you can see where RJ got the name&nbsp;
Mainstream Motors from. But anyway, his father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.120
had managed to raise $61 million over 25 years all&nbsp;
from the US government. So, his father was well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.760
aware of how to raise money, and given that the&nbsp;
US government was looking to support EV endeavors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.560
RJ was able to secure a small grant of 2 million&nbsp;
dollars. Given that he was building a car from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.920
scratch though, this really didn’t last that&nbsp;
long. RJ ended up spending $900,000 on payroll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.440
$170,000 on contractors, and the rest was&nbsp;
presumably on materials and manufacturing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.800
By 2011, RJ had burned through all the money,&nbsp;
but at least he had something to show for it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:07.040
Mainstream Motors had created an electric&nbsp;
sports car called the R1, but there was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:13.680
massive problem: the Tesla roadster. RJ’s sports&nbsp;
car wasn’t bad by any means, but the Roadster was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.840
already on the road and it didn’t make sense to&nbsp;
compete against Tesla in an already niche market.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.320
I’m not sure why RJ didn’t realize this&nbsp;
when he started the project as Tesla was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.280
delivering roadsters since 2008. But, he did&nbsp;
eventually make this realization and he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.360
decide to scrap the entire idea. Now, I’m&nbsp;
sure people are going to comment down below&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.800
that Rivian is considering bringing back this&nbsp;
car today, so it wasn’t a waste. But in 2011,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:45.840
the revival of this car was by no means a&nbsp;
guarantee. So, RJ was back to ground zero.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.240
CHANGING COURSE:&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.160
Determined to change the direction of the&nbsp;
company, RJ looked at what EV competitors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.080
weren’t targeting, and the obvious&nbsp;
answer was SUVs and pick up trucks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.960
RJ also decided to change the name of the company&nbsp;
to Rivian which was derived from Indian River.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.520
He combined the first part of River and the&nbsp;
last part of Indian. RJ had spent a lot of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.800
childhood in a rowboat on the Indian River in&nbsp;
Florida, hence the name. Anyway, RJ had a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:18.480
target and new name, but he was still lacking the&nbsp;
biggest part which was new funding. For RJ though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.080
this wasn’t that hard to secure. The source of&nbsp;
Rivian’s 2012 funding effort isn’t clear, but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.840
was likely the government again or some venture&nbsp;
capitalists who like to keep a low profile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.800
Over the next couple of years, Rivian hired a&nbsp;
bunch of talent from legacy automakers like Ford,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:38.960
GM, and Chrysler, and by the end of 2016,&nbsp;
they had grown to 100 employees. This is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.280
relatively small, but given that basically all&nbsp;
of these guys were engineers earning 6 figures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:48.320
it wasn’t cheap to run Rivian. Even if we&nbsp;
just assume $100,000 per year per person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.080
we’re looking at $10 million annually&nbsp;
on just payroll. And keep in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:58.480
Rivian still had no revenue coming in. Rivian was&nbsp;
also investing heavily into manufacturing plants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.760
For example, in January of 2017, Rivian acquired&nbsp;
a manufacturing plant from Mitsubishi for $16&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:09.120
million. Soon enough, Rivian revealed their pickup&nbsp;
truck and their SUV originally called the A1T&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:14.160
and the A1C at the LA Auto Show in November&nbsp;
of 2018. Unlike the Cybertruck reveal which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.440
left the audience divided, the A1T and A1C were&nbsp;
exactly what the audience wanted. From a distance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.080
they looked just like traditional vehicles, but&nbsp;
up close, they had that futuristic electric touch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.520
and that’s what made all the difference. Step&nbsp;
by step, Rivian was slowly getting ready to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:31.360
launch their first vehicle, but the last step&nbsp;
of bringing the product to market would take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.920
way longer and cost way more than anybody&nbsp;
expected. Fortunately for Rivian though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.880
investors with massive pockets would&nbsp;
enter the scene after this reveal.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:42.720
SMART MONEY:&nbsp;

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:46.720
Up until this point, Rivian had primarily&nbsp;
raised money in the tens of millions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.680
but it didn’t take long for them to cross into&nbsp;
the hundreds of millions. In May of 2018, Rivian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.840
took on $200 million worth of debt from Standard&nbsp;
Chartered bank which increased their total raised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:02.000
funds to a whopping $450 million. Despite raising&nbsp;
nearly half a billion dollars, the general public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.120
still wasn’t that interested in EVs as the price&nbsp;
was still way out of reach for most people. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:12.240
all of this would change with the launch of the&nbsp;
Tesla model 3 in 2017. While the Tesla model 3 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.080
a promising idea from the start, many big players&nbsp;
weren’t convinced that Tesla would actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.800
be able to execute on the idea. And this was an&nbsp;
absolutely fair assessment given that Tesla would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:24.080
go through production hell in 2018 trying to ramp&nbsp;
up the model 3. Tesla played with the bankruptcy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:27.920
line several times this year, and there were&nbsp;
plenty of customer complaints regarding subpar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.440
manufacturing. Despite all the uncertainty though,&nbsp;
Tesla survived 2018, and that was the signal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:38.880
that the time for EVs had finally come. Many big&nbsp;
players didn’t want to take the gamble with Tesla,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.880
but now that Tesla had gotten to the otherside,&nbsp;
they were willing to take the risk with other EV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:48.480
startups. And this led them straight to Rivian.&nbsp;
In February of 2019, Amazon led a $700 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:53.280
investment round for Rivian. Overnight Rivian&nbsp;
went from lifetime fundraising of $450 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:59.360
to raising $700 million in a single round and this&nbsp;
was just the beginning. Just two months later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:04.880
Ford invested $500 million which they would&nbsp;
later raise to $1.2 billion. Later that year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.680
Cox Automotive poured in another $350 million.&nbsp;
And Amazon would put the nail in the coffin by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:14.880
ordering 100,000 electric delivery vehicles from&nbsp;
Rivian. By the end of 2019, Rivian had raised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:20.720
a total of $2.85 billion, and now that smart&nbsp;
money was in, it was time to open up the gates.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.480
EV BUBBLE:&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:30.240
As we all know, starting at the end of 2019, Tesla&nbsp;
stock soured. First it crossed a $100 billion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.360
then it overtook Volkswagen and Toyota, and now&nbsp;
it’s literally a trillion dollar company. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:39.440
more than the rest of the top 10 auto companies&nbsp;
combined. I’m not trying to get into whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.760
that’s justified or not, but something that’s&nbsp;
crystal clear is the fact that Tesla took the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:48.560
of the EV industry with them and that of course&nbsp;
includes Rivian. In the meantime, Rivian was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.880
struggling to start production and get deliveries&nbsp;
going. Promised delivery dates and came and went,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:57.520
and Rivian kept delaying the release time after&nbsp;
time. But one thing we can be sure of was that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.320
money was no longer the issue. They had already&nbsp;
raised billions, and billions more were flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:07.840
in due to Tesla hype. But Rivian was running out&nbsp;
of time. Ford had revealed their F150 lightning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:11.840
and Tesla was rapidly building their Austin&nbsp;
gigafactory and making the cybertruck a reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:17.120
It would’ve been a shame if Rivian had targeted&nbsp;
the EV pick up truck and SUV market a decade ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.520
just to beat by Tesla and Ford. Fortunately&nbsp;
for Rivian though, they were able to deliver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:26.800
at the last second. At the end of August, Rivian&nbsp;
filed for an $80 billion IPO and this confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:31.120
that Rivian was finally ready to start making&nbsp;
deliveries. Ironically, despite targeting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.320
market years before Ford and Tesla, it looks like&nbsp;
they only beat them to market by months. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:41.680
by the time Rivian IPOd, they had raised&nbsp;
a total of $10.5 billion since 2019 alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:46.480
To put that in perspective, that’s half the&nbsp;
valuation of Nissan, twice the valuation of Mazda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:51.040
and four times the valuation of Aston Martin.&nbsp;
And all of that was just to get their first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.600
product to market. But looking back, that&nbsp;
was just a drop in the bucket given that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:01.440
would reach a valuation of $150 billion which&nbsp;
just leaves the question, what happens next?

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.280
FUTURE OF RIVIAN:&nbsp;

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:10.480
The truth is Rivian’s entire existence has been a&nbsp;
bubble. First it was millions from the government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:15.280
then it was tens of millions from early investors,&nbsp;
then it was hundreds of millions from smart money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:20.560
and now it's billions from the public markets.&nbsp;
It seems like this must come to an end soon, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:25.520
the truth is, that’s not necessarily the case. All&nbsp;
it takes is one announcement from Elon that Tesla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:30.800
is going to do a stock split on December 9, and&nbsp;
Tesla and EV industry will go to Mars. If Tesla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:35.680
makes another run, I wouldn’t be surprised if&nbsp;
Rivian ends up overtaking Toyota which is stupid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:40.480
but reality nonetheless. When the bubble does&nbsp;
eventually pop though, whether that's tomorrow or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:44.800
after Rivian reaches a trillion dollar valuation,&nbsp;
retail investors will likely lose substantial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.280
amounts of money. Instead of trashing on Rivian&nbsp;
and shorting the stock though, I think it's a much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.840
better idea to see it in a positive light. The EV&nbsp;
bubble has given companies that would otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.240
have little chance against the legacy automakers&nbsp;
an opportunity. And at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.680
the bubble is centered on a great cause which&nbsp;
is reducing pollution and transitioning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.680
sustainable energy. The more companies that&nbsp;
enter the scene and fight for market share,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:11.360
the faster we’ll see a transition to EVs. So,&nbsp;
maybe the bubble isn’t actually all that bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:16.000
The crash, however, will be deadly for Rivian&nbsp;
if they don’t make a mark before it’s too late.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.880
So, I wish the best to Rivian despite their&nbsp;
stupid valuation, but only time will tell if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.960
they’re able to make it to the other side. Do&nbsp;
you guys think Rivian will survive the eventual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:30.000
crash and rival Tesla? Comment that down below.&nbsp;
Also, drop a like if you also have a love hate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.480
relationship with the EV bubble. And of course,&nbsp;
consider joining our discord community to suggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:38.080
future video ideas and consider subscribing&nbsp;
to see more questions logically answered.

